From e38a75c83a7be9b5ad22b1e093814f59c4cf021e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:32:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 090/152] dt-bindings: extcon: sm5502: Add USB switch GPIO and
 role switch port

On Samsung tablets the SM5504 serves the pogo connector only. A dock is
identified by its ID resistor (34k or 49.9k), and the board then routes
the USB data lines of the host controller to the pogo pins with a GPIO
controlled switch and puts the controller into host mode.

Describe the switch GPIO and an OF graph port to the USB role switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/extcon/siliconmitus,sm5502-muic.yaml | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/extcon/siliconmitus,sm5502-muic.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/extcon/siliconmitus,sm5502-muic.yaml
index 7ef2d9bef..8a626beb1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/extcon/siliconmitus,sm5502-muic.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/extcon/siliconmitus,sm5502-muic.yaml
@@ -34,6 +34,21 @@ properties:
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  usb-switch-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      GPIO of an external switch that routes the USB data lines of the host
+      controller to the connector served by this MUIC instead of the main
+      USB port. It is asserted while a dock (ID resistor 34k or 49.9k on the
+      SM5504) is attached, as on the pogo connector of Samsung tablets.
+
+  port:
+    $ref: /schemas/graph.yaml#/properties/port
+    description:
+      Link to the USB controller's role switch. While a dock is attached the
+      controller is put into host mode, afterwards its previous role is
+      restored.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
-- 
